// spec: String has no `+=` on purpose (docs/stdlib/text.md, design.md 14): `s += t` is an error that says so and what to write, `<<`, which appends; WString alike
// found by thread E's battery (2026-11-06): the error said "codegen does not support String has no operator+= yet", as if it were a gap
// error: string_plus_assign_is_error.kpp:9: error: String has no operator+=: `<<` appends to a String
int main()
{
  String s("a");
  String t("b");
  s << t;
  s += t;
  println(s);
  return 0;
}
